cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "CorrelationPro: a browser-based platform for correlation analysis of every kind, with its theory"
abstract: >-
  CorrelationPro is a self-contained web application for correlation analysis that runs entirely
  in the browser, with no installation, no server-side computation and no third-party libraries.
  It reads spreadsheets, CSV, TSV and pasted text with its own reader, records the kind and role of
  each column, checks the assumptions of each pair and recommends a coefficient for each one. It
  computes every coefficient that applies to two variables with exact, asymptotic or permutation
  tests, analytic and bootstrap intervals and the Bayes factor; correlation matrices with
  multiple-testing corrections, the nearest positive-definite matrix, shrinkage and glyphs for up
  to a thousand variables; nonlinear dependence and copulas; partial, multiple and canonical
  correlation, RV, Procrustes, co-inertia and Mantel; categorical, ordinal and latent
  correlations; agreement and reliability; data with structure (groups, repeated measures, time
  series, space, phylogeny, angles and compositions); correlation networks; and the comparison of
  correlations, correction for attenuation and range restriction, power and meta-analysis. A
  reading in plain words accompanies each number, the home page explains the theory with labs that
  run the real engine, and the program ends in publication figures, palettes, a correlation table
  and a methods section written from what was actually run. Every engine of Blocks 1 to 12 was
  checked against independent implementations in R (19,334 comparisons, no disagreement).
